Package: spseg
Version: 0.9.0.9000
Date: 2026-10-19
Title: Measuring Spatial and Network Segregation
Author: Seong-Yun Hong <syhong@khu.ac.kr> and David O'Sullivan, with code 
  contributions by Benjamin Jarvis and Changlock Choi
Maintainer: Seong-Yun Hong <syhong@khu.ac.kr>
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: sf, stats, terra
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo, BH (>= 1.84.0-0)
Suggests: ggplot2, knitr, dplyr, tidyr, rmarkdown, roxygen2, sfnetworks,
        testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Encoding: UTF-8
Description: Measuring spatial segregation for categorical, ordinal,
        grouped-continuous, and observed-continuous variables in individual
        or aggregated population data. Calculates dissimilarity, information
        theory, relative diversity, root-family, and exposure/isolation indices
        using shared spatial searches for fixed-radius and population-count
        nearest-neighbor environments. Supports Euclidean distances and supplied
        networks with shortest-path hop counts or nonnegative traversal costs.
        Supports spatial geometries, coordinate
        columns, and count-preserving grid and pycnophylactic population surfaces.
        The framework builds on Reardon and Firebaugh (2002)
        <doi:10.1111/1467-9531.00110>, Reardon and O'Sullivan (2004)
        <doi:10.1111/j.0081-1750.2004.00150.x>, and Reardon (2009)
        <doi:10.1108/S1049-2585(2009)0000017011>.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/bfjarvis/spseg
NeedsCompilation: yes
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
